{
  "$comment": [
    "Terminology the translator must use, so the same English word does not",
    "become three different Uzbek words across three screens. Consulted by",
    "scripts/i18n-translate.mjs and enforced by scripts/i18n-validate.mjs.",
    "",
    "Product names stay in English ('Medly'), and so do clinical",
    "abbreviations written identically in all three languages, and 'Email',",
    "which both target locales already leave as-is.",
    "",
    "'AI' and 'Premium' ARE translated — ИИ and Премиум in Russian — so they",
    "live in `terms` with their required rendering rather than being listed",
    "here as protected. Listing a word that should be translated is how you",
    "end up with 'Премиум' flagged as an error."
  ],
  "doNotTranslate": [
    "Medly",
    "Medly AI",
    "Email",
    "CURB-65",
    "SpO₂",
    "GCS",
    "ECG",
    "MRI",
    "CT"
  ],
